🟠 9. Docker Engine & Storage
# Docker Engine
Docker Engine Docker ka core runtime environment hai jo containers ko build, run aur manage karta hai. Ye Docker platform ka main component hai.

Why Docker Engine is Used?
Containers create aur run karne ke liye
Images manage karne ke liye
Networking aur storage handle karne ke liye
Docker commands execute karne ke liye

 # Docker Daemon

Docker Daemon (dockerd) ek background service hai jo Docker Engine ka main process hota hai. Ye Docker requests ko receive karke containers, images aur networks ko manage karta hai.

Why Docker Daemon is Used?
Docker commands process karne ke liye
Containers manage karne ke liye
Images build aur run karne ke liye
Background me Docker operations execute karne ke liye

# Docker Storage Drivers

Storage Drivers Docker Images aur Containers ke layers ko manage karte hain. Ye decide karte hain ki data disk par kaise store hoga.

Why Storage Drivers are Used?
Image layers manage karne ke liye
Faster container creation ke liye
Efficient disk usage ke liye
Layer sharing aur caching ke liye

Common Storage Drivers:

overlay2
aufs
devicemapper
btrfs

# Docker Data Storage

Container ka data store karne ke process ko Docker Data Storage kehte hain.

Normally container delete hone par uska data bhi delete ho jata hai.

Why Data Storage is Used?
Important data save rakhne ke liye
Databases ke data ko persist karne ke liye
Container restart ke baad bhi data preserve karne ke liye

# Backup Containers

Container ke data aur configuration ka backup lena Backup Containers kehlata hai.

Why Backup is Used?
Data loss prevent karne ke liye
Disaster recovery ke liye
Production environment protection ke liye
Application restore karne ke liye

# Manage Storage

Docker storage resources jaise volumes, images aur container data ko monitor aur maintain karna Manage Storage kehlata hai.

Why Storage Management is Used?
Disk space optimize karne ke liye
Unused data remove karne ke liye
Performance improve karne ke liye
Storage utilization control karne ke liye


🟠 10. Docker Networking
Docker Networking Basics

Docker Networking containers ko ek dusre aur external world ke saath communicate karne ki facility provide karti hai.

Har container ko network connectivity di jati hai jisse applications communicate kar sakein.

Why Docker Networking is Used?
Container communication ke liye
Service connectivity ke liye
Internet access provide karne ke liye
Distributed applications run karne ke liye

# Docker Ports

Ports container ke application ko host machine ya external users ke liye accessible banate hain.

Why Ports are Used?
Application expose karne ke liye
User access provide karne ke liye
Web services run karne ke liye
External communication enable karne ke liye

Example:
Container ke andar application port 80 par chal rahi hai aur host par port 8080 se access ki ja sakti hai.

# Bridge Network

Bridge Docker ka default network driver hai jo ek hi host par running containers ko connect karta hai.

Why Bridge Network is Used?
Container-to-container communication ke liye
Isolated network create karne ke liye
Default Docker networking provide karne ke liye

# Host Network

Host Network me container directly host machine ka network use karta hai.

Isme container ka apna separate network namespace nahi hota.

Why Host Network is Used?
Better network performance ke liye
Low latency communication ke liye
Direct host network access ke liye

# Overlay Network

Overlay Network multiple Docker hosts ke containers ko connect karta hai.

Ye mostly Docker Swarm aur distributed environments me use hota hai.

Why Overlay Network is Used?
Multi-host communication ke liye
Distributed applications ke liye
Cluster environments ke liye

# Create Network

Docker me custom network create karke containers ko logically group kiya ja sakta hai.

Why Custom Network is Used?
Better isolation ke liye
Security improve karne ke liye
Application-specific communication ke liye

# Connect Containers

Containers ko same network me connect karke unke beech communication establish kiya jata hai.

Why Container Connection is Used?
Frontend aur backend communication ke liye
Application services connect karne ke liye
Database access provide karne ke liye

# Container Communication

Jab ek container dusre container se data exchange karta hai, ise Container Communication kehte hain.

Why Container Communication is Important?
Microservices architecture ke liye
Service interaction ke liye
Data sharing ke liye
Distributed applications ke liye

Example:
Frontend Container → Backend Container → Database Container

#  Default Bridge Network

Docker install hone ke baad automatically ek default bridge network create hota hai.

Agar koi custom network specify nahi kiya jata, to containers isi network par run hote hain.

Why Default Bridge Network is Used?
Basic container communication ke liye
Quick setup ke liye
Small applications ke liye
Default networking environment provide karne ke liye


> Interview Purpose (English)

Q: What is Docker Engine?
A: Docker Engine is the core runtime that builds, runs, and manages Docker containers.

Q: What is Docker Daemon?
A: Docker Daemon is a background service that manages Docker objects such as containers, images, networks, and volumes.

Q: Why do we use Docker Storage?
A: Docker Storage is used to persist and manage container data beyond the container lifecycle.

Q: What is Docker Networking?
A: Docker Networking enables communication between containers and external systems.

Q: What is a Bridge Network?
A: A Bridge Network is the default Docker network that allows containers on the same host to communicate.

Q: What is an Overlay Network?
A: An Overlay Network connects containers running on multiple Docker hosts.

Q: Why is Container Communication important?
A: It allows different services and microservices to interact and exchange data efficiently.